# regenerable outputs (built by the R/0x scripts; dirs recreated at runtime)
data/*
figures/*
!data/.gitkeep
!figures/.gitkeep
*.log

# cache/ and out/: same convention as module_3sp's top-level .gitignore entry --
# cache is large and fully regenerable (decay fits, edge lists), out/ keeps its
# receipts (the audit trail of what ran) but not the heavy .rds payloads.
# Two rds locations: the flat module_3sp-style stage receipt (out/<stage>/_receipt.rds)
# and, since 2026-09-04, module_sim's per-combination target subdirectory
# (out/<stage>/<tag_cell_rep>/_receipt.rds) -- both keep their receipt, neither
# keeps a payload .rds at that level.
cache/
out/*/*.rds
!out/*/_receipt.rds
out/*/*/*.rds
!out/*/*/_receipt.rds

# [!] cache/ and out/ ABOVE became SYMLINKS 2026-09-05 (PK: "use the external
# drive" -- the full reps x envs grid, 1400 combinations, filled both this
# machine's and mini2's internal disks; both now point at /Volumes/Nemo or
# /Volumes/T9). Git cannot see through a symlink to apply the directory-content
# rules above, and committing the symlink itself would point every other
# checkout at a path that only exists on this machine -- ignore it outright.
# results/ is the deliberate exception: small, git-trackable summaries copied
# out of the (now ignored) out/ tree, same convention as module_sim_LDscnR/results/.
/cache
/out
